[Event "Vienna: 2...Nf6 3.f4"]

{The Vienna develops the queen's knight first so that f2-f4 can come with more support. It is aggressive but sound.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nc3 {[%csl Gd5] The Vienna: supports e4 and keeps the f-pawn free for f4.}
2... Nf6 {Develops and hits e4. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
3. f4 {[%cal Gf4e5] The Vienna Gambit: White attacks e5 at once.}
3... d5 {The principled reply: counter in the centre.}
 (3... exf4 {Grabs the pawn but cedes the centre.}
4. e5 {[%cal Ge5f6] Kicks the knight. The pawn on e5 eyes the knight on f6.}
4... Ng8 {Back home; Black accepts a loss of time to keep the pawn.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and stops ...Qh4+. The knight on f3 controls d4.}
5... d6 {Strikes at e5. The pawn on d6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
6. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] Builds a big centre and opens the c1-bishop to take f4.}
)
4. fxe5 {Gains space and drives the knight once ...Nxe4.}
4... Nxe4 {The knight jumps to a central outpost. The knight on e4 eyes the knight on c3 and the pawn on d2.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and covers d4/h4. The knight on f3 controls d4.}
5... Be7 {Develops calmly.}
 (5... Nc6 {Develops and eyes e5. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
6. Bb5 {[%cal Gb5c6] Pins and pressures the defender of e5. The bishop on b5 eyes the knight on c6.}
)
6. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] Strong centre. White will play Bd3 and O-O.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3e4] Challenges the e4 knight. The bishop on d3 eyes the knight on e4.} *

[Event "Vienna: 2...Nc6 & 2...Bc5"]

{The Vienna can also be played positionally with Bc4, d3 and f4.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e5 {Classical. The pawn on e5 controls d4.}
2. Nc3 {The Vienna. The knight on c3 controls d5.}
2... Nc6 {Symmetrical development. The knight on c6 controls d4.}
 (2... Bc5 {Active bishop. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
3. Nf3 {Develops and attacks e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.}
3... d6 {Supports e5.}
4. Na4 {[%cal Ga4c5] Goes after the bishop. The knight on a4 eyes the bishop on c5.}
4... Bb6 {Keeps the bishop on the diagonal. The bishop on b6 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
5. Nxb6 {Wins the bishop pair. The knight on b6 eyes the rook on a8 and the bishop on c8 and controls d5.}
5... axb6 {Black gets the half-open a-file.}
6. d4 {[%csl Gd4] Opens lines for the bishops. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on e5.}
)
3. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4f7] Aims at f7. The bishop on c4 eyes the pawn on f7 and controls d5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 eyes the pawn on e4 and controls d5.}
4. d3 {[%csl Ge4] Solid: protects e4 and prepares f4.}
4... Bc5 {Active development. The bishop on c5 eyes the pawn on f2 and controls d4.}
5. f4 {[%cal Gf4e5] The thematic break, now well prepared. The pawn on f4 eyes the pawn on e5.}
5... d6 {Holds e5.}
6. Nf3 {Develops with pressure on e5. The knight on f3 eyes the pawn on e5 and controls d4.} *
